node_modules/
.mycoder/tmp/
dist/
# `pnpm pack` outputs. Both are *build* products, and both would otherwise make
# the tree dirty — which `collectBuildInfo` reads through `git status --porcelain`,
# so the next `pnpm pack --release` would refuse on the leftovers of the last one.
# `pack.ts` already unlinks `build-info.json` for exactly this reason; the tarball
# needed the same treatment and did not have it.
mycoder-*.tgz
build-info.json
coverage/
*.log
.DS_Store
# Ad-hoc eval runs are noise; a *released* artifact is evidence and must be
# readable by anyone the evidence matrix points at it. `scripts/evidence.ts`
# enforces the distinction: an `artifact:` reference to an untracked path is a
# failure, because "it exists on my machine" is not evidence.
# `evals/results/*` and not `evals/results/`: git cannot re-include anything under
# an excluded *directory*, so the negation below was inert and a released artifact
# had to be `git add -f`ed by hand. Excluding the entries rather than the directory
# is what makes `!` work — and what makes the rule below true rather than aspirational.
evals/results/*
!evals/results/release/
# An experiment artifact backing a documented conclusion has to be readable for the
# same reason a release artifact does: the numbers in the write-up are only checkable
# if the run behind them is.
!evals/results/experiments/
